/-!
# Tag 0B4X with no hypothesis beyond the situation's

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B4W] — a two-dimensional local normal Nagata domain `A` defining a
rational singularity, `S = Spec(A)`, and a modification `f : X ⟶ S` with `X` normal —
[Stacks, Tag 0B4X] asserts that `Hᵖ(X, ℱ) = 0` for `p ∉ {0, 1}` and every quasi-coherent
`𝒪_X`-module `ℱ`, and that `H¹(X, ℱ) = 0` when `ℱ` is generated by global sections.

Both clauses are proved here with no hypothesis beyond the data of the situation. The
cohomological input of the source's proof is [Stacks, Tag 02V7], which is proved in this
development for an arbitrary fibre dimension as
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FibreDimension.isZero_stalk_rightDerivedPlus_of_fiber_dimension_le`,
with its affine-base half
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FibreDimension.isZero_rightDerived_moduleGlobalSections_of_affine_base`.

## Main results

* `…TopDegreeBaseChange.isZero_rightDerivedPlus_moduleGlobalSections_of_noetherian_affine_base`:
  over an affine locally Noetherian base, a proper morphism whose fibres have dimension at most
  `d` has vanishing cohomology of *quasi-coherent* modules above `d`. This is the affine-base
  half of [Stacks, Tag 02V7] carried from coherent to quasi-coherent coefficients and read in
  the `rightDerivedPlus` indexing.
* The two clauses of [Stacks, Tag 0B4X] themselves are proved as
  `…RationalSingularitySituation.isZero_cohomology_of_notMem_zero_one_unconditional` and
  `…RationalSingularitySituation.isZero_cohomology_one_of_globallyGenerated_unconditional` of
  `QuasicoherentCohomologyExtra.lean` in this directory, and the tag is registered on their
  conjunction `…RationalSingularitySituation.isZero_cohomology_of_isQuasicoherent` there.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SemistableReduction.TwoModifications.isZero_cohomology_one_lt` and
  `…TwoModifications.isZero_cohomology_one_lt'`: the sentence *"Using the morphism `f : X → S`
  and the references above we find that `Hᵖ(X, ℱ) = 0` for `p > 1` for any coherent
  `𝒪_X`-module `ℱ`"* of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0AXF], on `X` and on `X'`. In degree two on
  `X` this is the right-hand exactness input of the short exact sequence of that tag.

## Implementation notes

Cohomology is `Hⁱ(X, ℱ) = ((moduleGlobalSections X).rightDerivedPlus i).obj ℱ`, the model used
throughout `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/TopDegreeBaseChange/`.

Three steps separate the affine-base half of [Stacks, Tag 02V7] from the shape the consumers in
this directory ask for. The degree moves from the `ℕ` of Mathlib's `Functor.rightDerived` to the
`ℤ` of `Functor.rightDerivedPlus` by `Stacks.DerivedIndexing.isZero_rightDerivedPlus_obj_iff`.
The coefficients move from coherent to quasi-coherent modules by
`…TopDegreeBaseChange.isZero_rightDerivedPlus_moduleGlobalSections_of_forall_isCoherent`, which
is the source's own last-paragraph reduction ([Stacks, Tags 01PK and 01FF]) and needs the source
to be locally Noetherian, quasi-compact and quasi-separated — all three consequences of `g` being
proper over an affine locally Noetherian base. And the fibre-dimension bound of the situation is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.topologicalKrullDim_fiber_le_natCast_one`,
respectively
`…SemistableReduction.TwoModifications.topologicalKrullDim_fiber_f'_le_one`.

The general lemma keeps `IsLocallyNoetherian` on the base, so it does not have the shape of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange.CohomologyVanishesAboveOne`, which quantifies over
an arbitrary affine base. The Noetherian case is what the consumers here need, the base being
`Spec(A)` for a Noetherian local ring `A`; clause (2) is therefore assembled from
`…TopDegreeBaseChange.isZero_rightDerivedPlus_one_of_generatingSections`, whose degree-two input
is a statement about the single morphism `f`, rather than from
`isZero_cohomology_one_of_generatingSections_of_fiber_dimension_le_one`, whose input is quantified
over every affine base.

`AlgebraicGeometry.moduleGlobalSections` and
`Stacks.Cohomology.AffineBase.moduleGlobalSections` are two names for the module-valued global
sections functor; the statements of this directory use the second, so the first is hidden from
the `open`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4X](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4X)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AXF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AXF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02V7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02V7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01FF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01FF)
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry hiding moduleGlobalSections
open Stacks.Cohomology.AffineBase

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange

attribute [local instance 10000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-- **The affine-base half of [Stacks, Tag 02V7] for quasi-coherent coefficients.** Let
`g : X₀ ⟶ Y₀` be proper onto an affine locally Noetherian scheme and suppose every fibre of `g`
has dimension at most `d`. Then `Hⁱ(X₀, ℱ) = 0` for every quasi-coherent `ℱ` and every `i > d`.

For *coherent* coefficients and in Mathlib's `ℕ` indexing this is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FibreDimension.isZero_rightDerived_moduleGlobalSections_of_affine_base`.
The passage to quasi-coherent coefficients is the source's own reduction, available as
`isZero_rightDerivedPlus_moduleGlobalSections_of_forall_isCoherent`: `X₀` is locally Noetherian
because `g` is of finite type over a locally Noetherian base, and quasi-compact and
quasi-separated because `g` is proper over an affine base. -/
theorem isZero_rightDerivedPlus_moduleGlobalSections_of_noetherian_affine_base
    {X₀ Y₀ : Scheme.{u}} (g : X₀ ⟶ Y₀) [IsProper g] [IsAffine Y₀] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y₀]
    {d : ℕ} (hfib : ∀ s : Y₀, topologicalKrullDim (g.fiber s) ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞))
    (F : X₀.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] (i : ℤ) (hi : (d : ℤ) < i) :
    IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections X₀).rightDerivedPlus i).obj F) := by
  have _ : IsLocallyNoetherian X₀ := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian g
  have _ : CompactSpace (X₀ : Type u) := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace g
  have _ : QuasiSeparatedSpace (X₀ : Type u) := quasiSeparatedSpace_of_quasiSeparated g
  refine isZero_rightDerivedPlus_moduleGlobalSections_of_forall_isCoherent X₀ i (by omega) F
    fun G hG => ?_
  have _ : G.IsCoherent := hG
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ : ∃ n : ℕ, i = (n : ℤ) :=
    ⟨i.toNat, (Int.toNat_of_nonneg (le_trans (Int.natCast_nonneg d) hi.le)).symm⟩
  rw [Stacks.DerivedIndexing.isZero_rightDerivedPlus_obj_iff (moduleGlobalSections X₀) hn]
  exact FibreDimension.isZero_rightDerived_moduleGlobalSections_of_affine_base
    g hfib G (by omega)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange

attribute [local instance 10000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable (S : RationalSingularitySituation.{u})

/-- The affine base of the situation is locally Noetherian: `A` is Noetherian because it is
Nagata. -/
instance isLocallyNoetherian_base : IsLocallyNoetherian S.base :=
  isLocallyNoetherian_Spec.mpr inferInstance

end AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.SemistableReduction.TwoModifications

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange

attribute [local instance 10000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable (S : TwoModifications.{u})

/-- The affine base of the situation is locally Noetherian. -/
instance isLocallyNoetherian_base : IsLocallyNoetherian S.base :=
  isLocallyNoetherian_Spec.mpr inferInstance

/-- The situation of [Stacks, Tag 0AXF] with the identity in place of `g`, so that the second
modification is `f` itself. This is how the bound on the fibres of `f` is read off the bound on
the fibres of the second modification. -/
abbrev toIdentity : TwoModifications.{u} where
  situation := S.situation
  X' := S.X
  g := 𝟙 S.X
  modification' := by
    change IsModification (𝟙 S.X ≫ S.f)
    rw [Category.id_comp]
    exact S.situation.modification
  normal := S.normal

/-- **The cohomological input of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0AXF] on `X'`.** In the situation of
that tag, `Hᵖ(X', ℱ) = 0` for every quasi-coherent `𝒪_{X'}`-module `ℱ` and every `p > 1`: the
morphism `f' = g ≫ f` is proper onto the affine Noetherian base `Spec(A)` and all of its fibres
have dimension at most one. -/
theorem isZero_cohomology_one_lt' (F : S.X'.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] (p : ℤ) (hp : 1 < p) :
    IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections S.X').rightDerivedPlus p).obj F) :=
  isZero_rightDerivedPlus_moduleGlobalSections_of_noetherian_affine_base S.f'
    (d := 1) (fun y => by simpa using S.topologicalKrullDim_fiber_f'_le_one y) F p (by omega)

/-- **The cohomological input of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0AXF] on `X`.** In the situation of
that tag, `Hᵖ(X, ℱ) = 0` for every quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `ℱ` and every `p > 1`.

Applied to `ℱ = g_*𝒪_{X'} = 𝒪_X` in degree two this is the vanishing that makes the second Leray
edge map of `g` surjective, which is the right-hand exactness of the short exact sequence of
[Stacks, Tag 0AXF]. -/
theorem isZero_cohomology_one_lt (F : S.X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] (p : ℤ) (hp : 1 < p) :
    IsZero (((moduleGlobalSections S.X).rightDerivedPlus p).obj F) := by
  refine isZero_rightDerivedPlus_moduleGlobalSections_of_noetherian_affine_base S.f
    (d := 1) (fun y => ?_) F p (by omega)
  have h : topologicalKrullDim ((𝟙 S.X ≫ S.f).fiber y) ≤ 1 :=
    S.toIdentity.topologicalKrullDim_fiber_f'_le_one y
  rw [Category.id_comp] at h
  simpa using h

end AlgebraicGeometry.SemistableReduction.TwoModifications

end

end
